{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794944552,"nonce":"skZgrfikgZxunGbr1HB21USSMbw=","message":"Physical iPhone AAC checks now pass on the connected iPhone 12 Pro Max (iOS 26.7.3) through hxcpp and Ash AOT. Both runtimes decoded/transferred/consumed all 49,152 frames from the normal 48-packet fixture. EOF, explicit pause/resume and default-output reopening passed. Native output reported an approximately 18.3 ms backend latency estimate; this is not acoustic loopback timing.\n\nBoth runtimes also passed the longer AAC-only listening fixture: 376 AAC-LC packets, exactly 385,024 frames consumed, a bounded 4,096-frame output ring, and generated PCM voices muted. Human listening confirmation was requested separately and is still pending for both iPhone runs. Do not infer audibility from these metrics or from the earlier confirmed Pixel tests.\n\nThe physical-iOS CLI path is implemented locally in hxn-audio: hxn audio check hl|cpp --av --target aarch64-apple-ios --device \u003cid\u003e --team \u003cid\u003e, with HXN_APPLE_TEAM as an alternative. It uses a dedicated UIKit test app, explicit development-team selection, Xcode automatic development signing and devicectl console verification/cleanup. hxcpp links its static archive; Ash --build supplies the AOT framework and its target runtime. A new target runtime was built from existing Ash source without editing it. Device signing details and identifiers are confined to generated test artifacts; committed templates contain none. The app identifier is dedicated to this test and does not replace an unrelated application. Every test app was uninstalled after completion. System volume was not adjusted.\n\nThe new CLI helper, app templates, README, design/convention docs and skill are uncommitted. Haxe formatter, Rust formatting/workspace tests, device-free DSP/mailbox regressions, skill validation and both generated Xcode project/plist checks pass. Normal hxn packaging was verified to ship the physical-iOS helper, templates and native archives in a haxelib without source Cargo files. Temporary listening data/settings were restored. Mobile-browser physical playback, real headset/route/interruption/focus transitions, acoustic loopback and Windows/Linux CI remain separate unverified work.","files":null}]}